Intentionally empty: firebase.json points `hosting.public` here.

Firebase Hosting requires a public directory, but this app must not have one with
files in it. Anything Hosting serves directly bypasses Next, and next.config.ts
defines headers that matter — /sw.js needs Content-Type, Cache-Control: no-store and
Service-Worker-Allowed: / or the service worker cannot claim root scope. Serving
public/ from the CDN would silently drop those.

So every request falls through to the Cloud Run rewrite and Next answers it, headers
included. This file is a dotfile, which Hosting's default `ignore` skips, so the
deploy uploads nothing at all.
